    port:eda-cace \
    port:py-gdstk \
    port:magic \
    port:netgen-lvs \
    port:klayout \
    port:xcircuit \
    port:gtkwave \
    port:py-volare \
    port:skim-app

destroot {
    xinstall -d ${destroot}${prefix}/share/doc/${name}
    system "echo '${name} ${version}: metaport for the macportseda sky130 toolchain.' \
        > ${destroot}${prefix}/share/doc/${name}/README"
}

notes "
eda-icall pulls in the MacPorts side of the sky130 toolchain. Things it
cannot do for you (see the macportseda README for details):

  1. Dependency variants must be right BEFORE the X11/GUI tools build:
       tk +x11 (not +quartz), gtk2 +quartz, cairo/pango +quartz+x11.
  2. The LibreLane RTL-to-GDS driver is a Python venv, not a port:
       uv venv --python 3.12 ~/.venvs/librelane
       ~/.venvs/librelane/bin/pip install librelane
     plus the 'librelane' wrapper script (PATH: venv, then
     ${prefix}/libexec/openroad-ll/bin, then ${prefix}/bin) and
     PDK_ROOT=~/.volare. LibreLane needs yosys built with +pyosys.
  3. Source builds of openroad/openroad-ll need the shadowing gates
     (deactivate boost spdlog protobuf3-cpp OpenSTA; reactivate after).
     Binary-less first installs of this metaport hit that on fresh machines.
  4. X11 GUIs (xschem, magic, netgen-lvs, xcircuit) need XQuartz.
  5. The simulator is the pinned eda-ngspice (ngspice 46): the binary is
     'eda-ngspice', or put ${prefix}/libexec/eda/bin early in PATH to get it
     as plain 'ngspice'. (The stock MacPorts ngspice port coexists and owns
     ${prefix}/bin/ngspice if installed.)
  6. eda-cace (the analog characterization engine, 'cace' / 'cace-web')
     needs PDK_ROOT pointing at a sky130A build at RUN time, same as the
     LibreLane flow above. It pulls py-ciel, the maintained successor to
     py-volare; both are installed and can coexist.
  7. FRESH MACHINE: the 'failed to fetch archive' messages from
     packages.macports.org are NORMAL -- no port in this tree has a prebuilt
     binary archive, so MacPorts just builds from source. Do NOT disable
     binaries. A FATAL fetch error is a distfile problem instead: restore the
     tree's distfiles archive first and the whole toolchain installs with no
     network at all --
       sudo rsync -a distfiles/ ${prefix}/var/macports/distfiles/
"

livecheck.type      none
